


Throttling is a technique used to control the rate of execution of a function or process. It ensures that a function is executed at most once in a specified time interval, even if it is triggered multiple times within that period.

Throttling is commonly used in web development, networking, and APIs to prevent excessive resource consumption.



Key Differences
Feature	               Throttling	                            Debouncing
Execution	           Ensures execution at regular intervals	Executes only after a delay once the event stops
Ignores Extra Calls?   Yes, within the interval	                Yes, until the delay is met
Use Cases	           Scrolling, window resizing, API calls	Search input, form validation, button clicks




Error Code - 429 -> to many requests
